  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>O Créol' is a family-run restaurant on the harbour in Hyères, at 6 avenue de la Gavine. Its official website presents Creole, Caribbean and world cuisine, with a sunny terrace overlooking the harbour. Dishes suit both adults and children: hot sauces and chillies are served separately on request. The menu includes vegetarian, vegan, gluten-free and lactose-free options, and every dish is also available to take away.</p>

      <h2>With your dog</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's official website lists "Pets friendly" among its features, next to the terrace, air conditioning and access for people with reduced mobility. This comes from the restaurant itself. It does not say whether dogs may enter the dining room, what size or how many dogs are accepted, and does not mention a water bowl: ask when booking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book a terrace table on 06 17 80 84 58, the number published by the restaurant, and mention that you are coming with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Opening hours</h2>
      <p>The restaurant serves from 11:45am to 2pm and from 7pm to 10pm on Monday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday and Sunday. It is closed on Tuesday and Wednesday. It also welcomes groups and can be privatised for an event.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The harbour area of Hyères and the Giens peninsula to the south offer seaside walks. Rules for dogs on beaches vary by municipality and season: check before you go.</p>
